{"seq": 1, "ts": 1793430266.17, "type": "add", "item": {"id": "at-0001", "kind": "lesson", "type": "code_convention", "topic": "money-rounding", "title": "Round money only with round_money", "content": "Always round monetary Decimal results with ledgerly.money.round_money (half-up to the cent); never use Python's round() or a bare Decimal.quantize(), which use banker's rounding and produce wrong invoice totals.", "scope": {"repo": "ledgerly", "observed_version": "1.0.0", "valid_from": "1.0.0", "valid_until": null, "files": ["ledgerly/invoice.py"]}, "source": {"task_id": "E01", "first_pass": false, "review_comments": ["[team convention] Round money only with ledgerly.money.round_money (half-up to the cent). Python's round() and a bare Decimal.quantize() use banker's rounding and give wrong invoice totals."], "references": []}, "evidence": [{"task_id": "E01", "version": "1.0.0", "source": {"kind": "review_comment", "quote": "Round money only with ledgerly.money.round_money (half-up to the cent). Python's round() and a bare Decimal.quantize() use banker's rounding and give wrong invoice totals.", "references": []}, "applied": {"kind": "code", "change": "added", "file": "ledgerly/invoice.py", "line": "return round_money(weighted_total / total_quantity)", "lines_matched": 1}, "verification": {"passed": true, "first_pass": false, "how": "hidden tests"}, "independent_review": null}, {"task_id": "E05", "version": "1.0.0", "source": {"kind": "diff", "quote": "return round_money(amount + amount * rate / Decimal(\"100\"))", "references": []}, "applied": {"kind": "code", "change": "added", "file": "ledgerly/pricing.py", "line": "return round_money(amount + amount * rate / Decimal(\"100\"))", "lines_matched": 1}, "verification": {"passed": true, "first_pass": true, "how": "hidden tests"}, "independent_review": null}], "status": "active", "supersedes": [], "superseded_by": null, "last_verification": {"task_id": "E05", "version": "1.0.0", "result": "passed", "how": "learned from a task whose final change passed verification"}, "usage": {"shown": 5, "cited": 3, "cited_pass": 2, "cited_fail": 1, "fail_streak": 0}, "last_failure": {"task_id": "E04", "review_comment": "[team convention] Every operation that moves money or changes a payment, credit or invoice balance must accept an optional keyword-only `idempotency_key=None` (callers without a key keep working). Check the key first, before validating state: if an audit entry with the same key already exists (ledgerly.audit.events()), return the original result (for functions that return a record, the same record) without applying the operation again. Include `idempotency_key` in the audit entry you write. Introduced after the double-refund incident INC-204."}}, "reason": "seeded from the main experiment's snapshot after the learning phase"}
{"seq": 2, "ts": 1793430266.171, "type": "add", "item": {"id": "at-0002", "kind": "lesson", "type": "code_convention", "topic": "money-normalization", "title": "Normalize money via to_money and round_money", "content": "Convert any monetary input with `to_money` from `ledgerly.money` and store it rounded with `round_money`; compare against `ZERO` rather than a literal Decimal.", "scope": {"repo": "ledgerly", "observed_version": "1.0.0", "valid_from": "1.0.0", "valid_until": null, "files": ["ledgerly/invoice.py"]}, "source": {"task_id": "E02", "first_pass": true, "review_comments": [], "references": []}, "evidence": [{"task_id": "E02", "version": "1.0.0", "source": {"kind": "diff", "quote": "price = to_money(unit_price)", "references": []}, "applied": {"kind": "code", "change": "added", "file": "ledgerly/invoice.py", "line": "line = LineItem(description, quantity, round_money(price))", "lines_matched": 1}, "verification": {"passed": true, "first_pass": true, "how": "hidden tests"}, "independent_review": null}, {"task_id": "E04", "version": "1.0.0", "source": {"kind": "diff", "quote": "amount = round_money(to_money(amount))", "references": []}, "applied": {"kind": "code", "change": "added", "file": "ledgerly/adjustments.py", "line": "payment.refunded_amount = round_money(refunded + amount)", "lines_matched": 1}, "verification": {"passed": true, "first_pass": false, "how": "hidden tests"}, "independent_review": null}], "status": "active", "supersedes": [], "superseded_by": null, "last_verification": {"task_id": "E05", "version": "1.0.0", "result": "passed", "how": "cited by a task whose first attempt passed verification"}, "usage": {"shown": 4, "cited": 2, "cited_pass": 1, "cited_fail": 0, "fail_streak": 0}}, "reason": "seeded from the main experiment's snapshot after the learning phase"}
{"seq": 3, "ts": 1793430266.171, "type": "add", "item": {"id": "at-0003", "kind": "lesson", "type": "code_convention", "topic": "billing-error-codes", "title": "Raise BillingError with stable snake_case codes", "content": "Reject invalid billing input by raising `BillingError(code, detail)` from `ledgerly.errors` with codes like `invalid_state`, `invalid_quantity`, `negative_amount`, matching the existing `issue_invoice` pattern.", "scope": {"repo": "ledgerly", "observed_version": "1.0.0", "valid_from": "1.0.0", "valid_until": null, "files": ["ledgerly/invoice.py"]}, "source": {"task_id": "E02", "first_pass": true, "review_comments": [], "references": []}, "evidence": [{"task_id": "E02", "version": "1.0.0", "source": {"kind": "diff", "quote": "raise BillingError(\"invalid_state\", f\"invoice {invoice.id} is {invoice.status}\")", "references": []}, "applied": {"kind": "code", "change": "added", "file": "ledgerly/invoice.py", "line": "raise BillingError(\"invalid_quantity\", repr(quantity))", "lines_matched": 1}, "verification": {"passed": true, "first_pass": true, "how": "hidden tests"}, "independent_review": null}, {"task_id": "E03", "version": "1.0.0", "source": {"kind": "diff", "quote": "from .errors import BillingError", "references": []}, "applied": {"kind": "code", "change": "added", "file": "ledgerly/renewals.py", "line": "raise BillingError(\"invalid_period\", repr(sub.period_days))", "lines_matched": 1}, "verification": {"passed": true, "first_pass": true, "how": "hidden tests"}, "independent_review": null}, {"task_id": "E05", "version": "1.0.0", "source": {"kind": "diff", "quote": "raise BillingError(\"invalid_tax_rate\", str(rate_percent))", "references": []}, "applied": {"kind": "code", "change": "added", "file": "ledgerly/pricing.py", "line": "raise BillingError(\"invalid_tax_rate\", str(rate_percent))", "lines_matched": 1}, "verification": {"passed": true, "first_pass": true, "how": "hidden tests"}, "independent_review": null}, {"task_id": "E06", "versi