{"seq": 6, "ts": 1793430266.171, "type": "add", "item": {"id": "at-0006", "kind": "lesson", "type": "process", "topic": "idempotency-key-convention", "title": "Money operations take keyword-only idempotency_key", "content": "Every function that moves money or changes a payment, credit or invoice balance must accept keyword-only `idempotency_key=None` and check it first, before state validation: if `ledgerly.audit.events()` already has an entry with that key, return the original record without reapplying. Pass `idempotency_key` into the `audit.record(...)` call.", "scope": {"repo": "ledgerly", "observed_version": "1.0.0", "valid_from": "1.0.0", "valid_until": null, "files": ["ledgerly/adjustments.py"]}, "source": {"task_id": "E04", "first_pass": false, "review_comments": ["[team convention] Every operation that moves money or changes a payment, credit or invoice balance must accept an optional keyword-only `idempotency_key=None` (callers without a key keep working). Check the key first, before validating state: if an audit entry with the same key already exists (ledgerly.audit.events()), return the original result (for functions that return a record, the same record) without applying the operation again. Include `idempotency_key` in the audit entry you write. Introduced after the double-refund incident INC-204.", "[team convention] Support-initiated refunds and credits above 500.00 need a second approver (finance policy FIN-2026-03): accept an optional keyword-only `approved_by=None` (callers that do not need approval keep working). Amounts at or below 500.00 need no approval; above it, raise BillingError(\"approval_required\") when `approved_by` is missing."], "references": ["INC-204"]}, "evidence": [{"task_id": "E04", "version": "1.0.0", "source": {"kind": "review_comment", "quote": "Every operation that moves money or changes a payment, credit or invoice balance must accept an optional keyword-only `idempotency_key=None`", "references": ["INC-204"]}, "applied": {"kind": "code", "change": "added", "file": "ledgerly/adjustments.py", "line": "def refund(payment, amount, at, *, idempotency_key=None, approved_by=None):", "lines_matched": 1}, "verification": {"passed": true, "first_pass": false, "how": "hidden tests"}, "independent_review": null}], "status": "active", "supersedes": [], "superseded_by": null, "last_verification": {"task_id": "E06", "version": "1.0.0", "result": "passed", "how": "cited by a task whose first attempt passed verification"}, "usage": {"shown": 1, "cited": 1, "cited_pass": 1, "cited_fail": 0, "fail_streak": 0}}, "reason": "seeded from the main experiment's snapshot after the learning phase"}
{"seq": 7, "ts": 1793430266.171, "type": "add", "item": {"id": "at-0007", "kind": "lesson", "type": "business_policy", "topic": "refund-approval-threshold", "title": "Refunds above 500.00 need approved_by", "content": "Per finance policy FIN-2026-03, support-initiated refunds and credits above 500.00 require a second approver: accept keyword-only `approved_by=None` and raise `BillingError(\"approval_required\")` when the amount exceeds the threshold and no approver is given. Amounts at or below 500.00 need no approval.", "scope": {"repo": "ledgerly", "observed_version": "1.0.0", "valid_from": "1.0.0", "valid_until": null, "files": ["ledgerly/adjustments.py"]}, "source": {"task_id": "E04", "first_pass": false, "review_comments": ["[team convention] Every operation that moves money or changes a payment, credit or invoice balance must accept an optional keyword-only `idempotency_key=None` (callers without a key keep working). Check the key first, before validating state: if an audit entry with the same key already exists (ledgerly.audit.events()), return the original result (for functions that return a record, the same record) without applying the operation again. Include `idempotency_key` in the audit entry you write. Introduced after the double-refund incident INC-204.", "[team convention] Support-initiated refunds and credits above 500.00 need a second approver (finance policy FIN-2026-03): accept an optional keyword-only `approved_by=None` (callers that do not need approval keep working). Amounts at or below 500.00 need no approval; above it, raise BillingError(\"approval_required\") when `approved_by` is missing."], "references": ["FIN-2026-03"]}, "evidence": [{"task_id": "E04", "version": "1.0.0", "source": {"kind": "review_comment", "quote": "Support-initiated refunds and credits above 500.00 need a second approver (finance policy FIN-2026-03)", "references": ["FIN-2026-03"]}, "applied": {"kind": "code", "change": "added", "file": "ledgerly/adjustments.py", "line": "if amount > APPROVAL_THRESHOLD and not approved_by:", "lines_matched": 1}, "verification": {"passed": true, "first_pass": false, "how": "hidden tests"}, "independent_review": null}], "status": "active", "supersedes": [], "superseded_by": null, "last_verification": {"task_id": "E04", "version": "1.0.0", "result": "passed", "how": "learned from a task whose final change passed verification"}, "usage": {"shown": 1, "cited": 0, "cited_pass": 0, "cited_fail": 0, "fail_streak": 0}}, "reason": "seeded from the main experiment's snapshot after the learning phase"}
